cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
authors:
  - name: RakTikoo
title: "ci-command-truth: prove every run: command in your GitHub workflows exists"
version: 0.4.1
date-released: 2026-11-19
license: MIT
url: "https://github.com/RakTikoo/ci-command-truth"
repository-code: "https://github.com/RakTikoo/ci-command-truth"
abstract: >-
  Statically checks that every run: command in a repository's GitHub
  workflows actually exists — the npm script, make target, or script file it
  names — so broken references are caught before CI runs, in milliseconds,
  with zero dependencies.
keywords:
  - GitHub Actions
  - CI
  - workflow
  - validation
  - static analysis
